ANNOTATION: "SEP-OTBN-ISA-NOT-CLAIMED: this is an OWNERSHIP/SCOPE waiver, not a structural unreachability claim. SEP exercises OTBN through its CSR and memory interfaces, not across the full BN.* instruction set. Instruction decode and the bignum ALU are verified by lowRISC's own OTBN DV; SEP DV does not claim them. The remaining OTBN logic -- the controller, the scramble control and the memory path -- stays graded because SEP tests drive it. Nothing in the SEP integration ties these arms off: otbn is elaborated in full with Stub(1'b0) and RegFile(RegFileFF) at hw/sys/sep/rtl/sep_crypto_otbn_wrapper.sv:161-165, so a firmware test that executed the missing instructions would cover them. Only the never-executed decode arms are listed; every line any SEP test reached stays in the denominator. NOT waived: otbn_controller, otbn_scramble_ctrl, otbn_core, otbn_reg_top and the OTBN memory path."
